## 13. Definition of done

- `npm run check` passes; no `TODO`, no `any`, no `@ts-ignore`, no `console.log` left in `src/`.
- On a 360×740 viewport, every tier renders without page scroll: header, trace strip, full grid and the chips are all visible; cells are ≥ 28px.
- Dragging from a letter draws a yellow pill that snaps to 8 directions and never flickers between two directions when the finger moves slowly near a sector boundary.
- Releasing on a listed word (either reading direction) locks the pill in a color, strikes the chip, and vibrates on Android Chrome; releasing on anything else fades the pill out with no other feedback.
- The page never scrolls, zooms, or triggers pull-to-refresh during a drag; long-press never selects text or shows a callout.
- Tapping a chip pulses the word's first letter; unlimited.
- Finding the last word shows the completion card; "Próxima fase" opens index+1; index 12 shows the theme-complete message.
- Reloading mid-puzzle restores found words with the same colors; the home screen shows correct "n de 12" counts and a "Continuar" row.
- Same puzzle key → identical grid on every device.
- Works offline after one load; installable from Chrome's menu; `lang="pt-BR"`; every user-visible string comes from `strings.ts`.
- Dark mode follows the system by default and can be forced in settings; `prefers-reduced-motion` disables animations.

